{"context":"Today an unsandboxed worker inherits the host environment and filesystem - an acknowledged risk. Steward spawns agent CLIs that may run arbitrary commands.","decision":"A worker sandbox is mandatory in v1: env allow-list reusing the existing `pluginEnv` mechanism, process-group spawn hardening, and checksum trust per ADR-028. Per-worker git-worktree isolation. ACP `session/request_permission` is answered default-deny, never hanging. No opt-out in v1.","consequences":"Workers cannot read the host env or escape their worktree by default; permission-requiring actions are denied until explicitly allowed. Safety is inherited from existing hardened patterns rather than invented. Cost: sandbox setup and worktree lifecycle; some prompts may need policy updates.","alternativesConsidered":"No sandbox (rejected: documented host risk). Opt-in sandbox (rejected: unsafe default). Container-per-worker (deferred: heavier; worktree + env allow-list chosen for v1).","appliesTo":["eka-steward/**"]}